And earcut.js signedArea:

```js
function signedArea(data, start, end, dim) {
    let sum = 0;
    for (let i = start, j = end - dim; i < end; i += dim) {
        sum += (data[j] - data[i]) * (data[i + 1] + data[j + 1]);
        j = i;
    }
    return sum;
}
```

Same as C++. So for a standard-CCW ring, sum > 0. Outer called with clockwise=true → true === true → forward. Holes with clockwise=false → false === true → false → reverse. That matches what I did.

